----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetStatusGrid` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block):
  it takes `cells: StatusCell[]` + optional `cols` (2|3|4) / `compact` / `emptyMessage` / `emptyIcon` and
  renders a responsive grid of status chips. Each chip = an optional leading icon + a truncated label over an
  optional value, a tone-tinted rounded border, and a small status dot pinned to the top-trailing corner
  (web `absolute right-2 top-2 size-2`). The grid COLLAPSES its column count by the widget's own rendered
  width (web container-query class table): cols 2 -> always 2; cols 3 -> 1 (<256) / 2 (>=256) / 3 (>=384);
  cols 4 -> 2 (<384) / 4 (>=384). `compact` forces 2 columns, suppresses the value line (web
  `!compact && cell.value`), and tightens the padding. Its only own branch is `cells.length === 0 ->
  <EmptyState message={emptyMessage} icon={emptyIcon} />`. There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the
  source, so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch (the host widget that owns the query renders
  those). Per the sibling presentational-primitive precedent (WidgetChartSummary 0002, WidgetComparisonCard
  0003) this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches:
    • populated grid    (one StatusGridCell per cell; responsive 2/3/4-up column collapse)
    • status tones      (ok->success, warning->warning, error->danger, inactive/unknown->neutral glass)
    • compact variant   (2 columns, value suppressed, tight padding)
    • empty leaf        (friendly "never a blank box" peer of web <EmptyState message emptyIcon/>)
  Files: WidgetStatusGrid.Adapter/Model/.swift/Views/Previews/Tests/AdapterTests.swift + .strings.
  Bindings : P1/S8 WidgetStatusGridModel @Observable holder (props + projection; no HTTP in the view);
             P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius) — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex;
             P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade (table "WidgetStatusGrid"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry
             (slug "WidgetStatusGrid", emitted once + idempotent across appear/disappear).
  i18n     : web source has 0 t() keys (anonymous; its only literal "No status data available" — the
             emptyMessage default — is reproduced via widgetStatusGrid.empty). Native a11y/HIG additions:
             emptyHint; spoken status words status.{ok,warning,error,inactive,unknown}; cellLabel /
             cellLabelNoValue combined readings. Every key the code resolves exists in the catalog; 0 dead.
  a11y     : each chip folds label+value into ONE VoiceOver element and RESTATES the status as a spoken word
             (so the color-coded dot is not the only status signal — colorblind/VoiceOver parity); the dot +
             decorative icon are accessibilityHidden; min-h 44 (HIG touch target); Dynamic Type via tokens;
             empty leaf is one combined element. ContentUnavailableView is the native EmptyState peer.

